The seminary was beginning to feel lonely as many of Mark's fellow
priests left on a holy crusade never to return.  After doing all of
the laundry and dishes, painting the fence and harvesting the crops,
Mark decided to attempt the holy task himself (well there was no one
left to volunteer).

On level 3 of the DoD, there was a lawful altar and an antique armour
shop with a pair of speed boots to hasten Mark along.  On level 4 he
Etched the floor with an unknown wand only to discover it was a wow
(0:2), so he stuck to the old favourite (2 bSoC, GDSM+3, GoD) and
saved some wishes for later (magic markers and an amulet of
reflection).

The early game was unique in the large number of tins of spinach.  The
mines were taken care of in quick attack and retreat runs.   Sokoban
gave a bag of holding.

The lawful temple on 12 provided 9 points of protection (over time).
Level 13 was a zoo and the quest portal.   The quest was a bout of
hacking and slashing as I had no pets at this point.   Most of my
armour had been enchanted prior to entering the quest.

My main stash was on level 16.  I left a great stockpile for future
adventurers (many divine artifact gifts from the god).  I left behind:
Demon bane, snickersnee and troll bane.

On level 22, there was a huge zoo, but the buffed up priest chewed
them up and spit the out without much pause.  The throne room on 24
gave nothing good.   I had found levitation boots to get across to
Medusa's island (Titan version).  The statue had boots of water
walking (these are cool).

The castle gave me the only major scare as a something started a
summoning spree including green slim, purple worm and  mind flayers.
Fortunately, I could caste charm monster very well and defeated the
enemies with some help from my many pets including some of the Purple
Worms (best pets ever).   The wand went for many more magic markers, a
T-shirt and a ring of slow digestion, as I was tired of having to stop
to eat all the time.   It was also at this point that I discovered
that a ring of sustain abilities also prevents you from gaining
strength from Giant meals (Duh!^%%#@#%$#%).

